        "reasoning_content": "You are a rater applying idea-evaluation instrument... Apply published anchored levels exactly...\n\nWe need rate proposal P2190.\n\nText: Automated Compliance Report Generator. A tool parses system logs to automatically populate technical documentation and record-keeping files required by Recital 71. It transforms raw telemetry into regulatory evidence. Build data pipeline maps specific log event IDs to corresponding requirements of Article 12 and exports them into standardized templates. Runs as part of CI/CD pipeline. Eliminates manual administrative burden on engineers during system validation phase.\n\nWe need six subscales.\n\noriginality: degree to which idea is not only rare but ingenious... 4 = not expressed before AND ingenious... 3 = unusual, interesting; shows some imagination 2 = interesting 1 = common mundane boring\n\nAutomated compliance report generator parsing logs to populate documentation. Is this common? In AI labs, automating compliance documentation from logs is fairly common practice? Probably interesting but not rare. Might be unusual? I'd say interesting but not ingenious. Many tools exist for log parsing and report generation. Could be 2 = interesting. Possibly 3 = unusual interesting shows some imagination. Hmm.\n\nRarity reference class: set of responses experienced evaluator would expect AI R&D labs to give to this mandate. Expected responses: build logging, hire compliance officer, manual documentation... Automated generator is somewhat expected. I'd say interesting but not rare. Maybe level 2.\n\nparadigm_relatedness (1-4): degree to which idea preserves or modifies paradigm anchored to this problem.\n4 = paradigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and its compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners or offerings born from compliance)\n