        "reasoning_content": "You are a rater applying idea-evaluation instrument... Apply published anchored levels exactly, one level per subscale, and give one sentence of evidence for each rating.\n\nWe need rating for proposal P1807.\n\nSubscales in order: applicability, effectiveness, implementability, acceptability, originality, paradigm_relatedness\n\nNeed one sentence evidence then score.\n\nProposal: Unified High-Risk Event Logging Middleware. Standardized software library automatically captures timestamps, input data, system events across all high-risk prototypes. Ensures consistent telemetry... decorator-based API in Python intercepts function calls to pipe metadata into immutable centralized database. Plug-and-play logging layer. Removes manual record-keeping burden, maintaining high prototyping velocity while guaranteeing compliance.\n\nApplicability (1-4): degree to which idea clearly applies to stated problem.\nProblem: AI R&D lab subject to regulation must decide how to respond: how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Approval means committing scarce implementation resources to pursue proposal, not funding to explore whether idea might someday work.\n\nProposal directly addresses logging mandate: automatic recording of events logs over lifetime, timestamps, input data, system events. Article 12 requires automatic recording of events logs, identifying situations risk etc. So solves identified problem directly related. Score 4.\n\nEvidence sentence: The middleware directly provides automatic event logging with timestamps and input capture required by Article 12 for high-risk prototypes.\n\nEffectiveness (1-4): degree to which idea will solve problem.\nReasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability? It captures timestamps, input data, system events across prototypes. Article 12 also requires specific items for point 1(a) Annex III: period of each use, reference database, input data for match, identification of