robably 4.\n\nImplementability (1-4): degree can be easily implemented.\nEasy to implement at low cost? Leadership effort to define industry-wide schemas, collaborate with EU institutions, publish white papers. That's some changes, reasonably feasible measures, not easy low cost. Might be 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures. Could be 2 = significant change expensive difficult. Team will publish open-source formats... That requires resources but plausible. I'd say 3.\n\nApplicability (1-4): degree clearly applies to stated problem.\nProblem: lab must decide how to respond: meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D. Proposal standardizes reporting, implement Article 12 transparently. Solves identified problem directly related? It helps meet logging mandate via standardization. Does it solve? It's about standards not internal implementation. Applicability maybe 3 = solves an implied problem that is related (do X to get implied Y). Or 4 = solves identified problem directly related. The stated problem is how to meet logging mandate. Standard schemas help meet mandate. Might be 3? Hmm.\n\nThe proposal aims to standardize how labs report... It increases scientific impact. Directly related to logging mandate. I'd say 4 = solves an identified problem that is directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem). Actually it doesn't guarantee lab meets its own logging, but it helps.\n\nMaybe applicability 3? Let's choose 3: solves implied problem of interoperability? Could be 4.\n\nEffectiveness (1-4): degree will solve problem.\nReasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability? Standard setting won't necessarily make this lab compliant; it's indirect. It contributes to solution but partial. So 3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution of problem (it helps, but only partial solution). Might be 2? I'd say 3.\n\nNeed one sentence evidence each.\n\nProvide output echo id.\n\nFormat: probably list.\n\nEnsure subscale_evidence then subscale.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid P1499\noriginality_evidence: ...\noriginality: 3\netc.\n\nMake sure order: originality, paradigm_relatedness, acceptability, implementability, applicability, effectiveness\n\nProvide evidence sentence first then score.\n\nLet's output.\n\n",
